course: dictionary
lesson: 12074
title: Climatic: weather over many years
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Climate is the usual weather of a place over many years. Climatic is the adjective that goes with it, so it tells you something is to do with climate. «Deserts have harsh climatic conditions, with very little rain all year.» The words all year and very little rain point to a pattern that lasts a long time.
explain: Look for clue words that show the time span. «Scientists are studying climatic change to see how the world's weather is shifting.» Shifting over years, not in one afternoon, tells you climatic is about long-term patterns. If the sentence is about one stormy day, climatic is probably the wrong word.
explain: A good check is to swap in a simpler phrase, such as "to do with climate". «The climatic zones of the world include tropical, desert and polar areas» still makes sense that way, so you have understood it.
fact: Climatic means to do with climate.
fact: Climate is the usual weather of a place over many years.
fact: Weather is what happens today; climate is what usually happens over years.
fact: «Climatic zones» are large areas with similar long-term weather, such as tropical, desert, temperate and polar.
fact: «Climatic change» means long-term changes in the weather of the world.
exercise: «Deserts have harsh climatic conditions.» What does climatic mean here? | To do with cooking food | To do with a single rainy day | * To do with the usual weather over many years | To do with sport
exercise: Scientists talk about «climatic change» in the news. What does this phrase mean? | A sudden storm on one afternoon | A special dinner menu | * Long-term changes in the weather of the world | A new type of car
exercise: Mia says weather and climate mean the same thing. What is the best answer? | They mean exactly the same thing | Weather is only about the sea | Climate is only about wind | * Weather is today's conditions, and climate is the usual pattern over many years
test: «The rainforest and the Arctic are in very different climatic zones.» What are climatic zones? | Times of day when the sun is up | Small gardens with flowers | * Large areas with similar long-term weather, such as tropical or polar
test: Ben says climatic means "happening right now". Is he right? | Yes, it means a sudden storm | * No, climatic means to do with the usual weather of a place over many years | Yes, it means today's weather
exam: Which sentence uses climatic correctly? | The bus was late, so the climatic arrival was at noon | * Scientists measure the climatic conditions of the Arctic over many years | Ella had a climatic headache after lunch | My climatic shoes are red and very comfy
